<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The hardened runtime is required for notarization, and it revokes microphone
    access unless this entitlement is present. The Info.plist usage strings are
    what TCC shows in the prompt; this is what makes the prompt reachable at all.

    Deliberately minimal. ONNX Runtime is statically linked into the binary
    (`otool -L` shows no onnx dylib), so none of the usual escape hatches —
    disable-library-validation, allow-unsigned-executable-memory, allow-jit —
    are needed. Anything added here is a hole in the runtime protections, so add
    one only after a real run has failed without it.

    System-audio capture via the Core Audio process tap needs no entitlement:
    it is gated on TCC plus NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription in the Info.plist.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
